This is the four-cell map you have just learned, but each box now shows the disciplinary breakdown from its study. Three of the four corners have a SCORE paper behind them: reproduction top-left, replication top-right, reanalysis bottom-left. The fourth, generalisation, we leave aside. Economics and political science lead on reproduction while sociology lags, replication hovers around half almost everywhere, and reanalysis holds the original conclusion three times in four. We take the three studies in turn, starting with reproduction.
